```

For an input of length L, insertion, search, and prefix checking each take O(L) average time. Space is O(S), where S is the total number of nodes created. The dictionary is convenient and supports any characters, but it has more per-entry overhead than a fixed 26-slot array.

I used `Map` for the child links so the structure does not reserve 26 positions at every node. The `findNode` method stops as soon as a character is missing. A complete word is different from a prefix because only the final node of an inserted word has `isWord` set.

An empty prefix is handled naturally: the root is returned, so `startsWith("")` is true. Inserting the same word again only sets the same flag again.

```javascript
class Trie {
    constructor() {
        this.children = new Map();
        this.isWord = false;
    }

    insert(word) {
        let node = this;

        for (const ch of word) {
            if (!node.children.has(ch)) {
                node.children.set(ch, new Trie());
            }
            node = node.children.get(ch);
        }

        node.isWord = true;
    }

    search(word) {
        const node = this.findNode(word);
        return node !== null && node.isWord;
    }

    startsWith(prefix) {
        return this.findNode(prefix) !== null;
    }

    findNode(text) {
        let node = this;

        for (const ch of text) {
            if (!node.children.has(ch)) {
                return null;
            }
            node = node.children.get(ch);
        }

        return node;
    }
}

